# Everything is LF in the repository, whatever the checkout platform does.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Scripts come in pairs: bash for macOS, Linux and Git Bash, PowerShell for
# Windows. PowerShell 5 misreads LF-only files in some cases; CRLF is safe for
# both 5 and 7.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary files are stored, diffed and merged byte for byte. text=auto alone
# decides by content, and a PDF with no NUL byte in its first 8000 bytes passes
# the diff and merge check for text: its diff runs to hundreds of thousands of
# lines, and a three-way merge of two versions would splice them line by line.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.sbt text eol=lf
*.scala text eol=lf
